<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Allied invasion of Sicily</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1943</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Allied invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> campaign in 1943 in which British, American and Canadian forces landed on and captured Sicily. The invasion contributed to the overthrow of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a> in July 1943. It was a key step in the collapse of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascist-italy">Fascist Italy</a> and the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/allied-invasion-of-sicily.jpg" alt="Allied invasion of Sicily" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Military Academy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_operation_husky_landing.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
